      "text": "{\"cards\":[{\"thesis\":\"A nonrefundable vehicle credit can disappear for moderate-income buyers after family credits, making a cheaper used car win after taxes.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"A posted tax credit always lowers the car's real price.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"For low-bracket workers receiving refundable family credits, pretax retirement contributions can reduce future flexibility without meaningfully lowering today's tax bill.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Pretax retirement saving is automatically the best tax move for every worker.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"Alternating charitable gifts into high-deduction filing periods can beat steady giving, even when total donations and cash flow stay unchanged.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"The tax benefit of giving depends only on total donated.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"Using a payroll-funded medical savings account often beats claiming medical deductions, because payroll taxes fall even when income deductions vanish.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Medical expenses mainly help at tax time through itemized deductions.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"Increasing paycheck withholding late in the year can prevent underpayment penalties more reliably than mailing catch-up estimated payments for gig income.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Late estimated payments fix underpayment penalties as well as paycheck withholding.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"For partners using marketplace health subsidies, marrying before year-end can raise combined tax owed versus staying unmarried until January, despite shared expenses.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Marriage almost always creates a tax bonus for committed partners.\\\"\"}]}"
